              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aestīvus, aestīva, aestīvum — \"of summer, summer\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Dīves vīllam aestīvam in montibus habet. The rich man has a summer house in the mountains."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An adjective of three endings, from aestās 'summer'. Aestīva (n. pl.), a summer camp. English aestivate comes from the same root."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aestīvus is built on aestās 'summer' with the suffix -īvus (EtymDB; Lewis & Short), and aestās goes back to PIE h₂eydʰ- 'to burn'."
            }
          ]
        },
